Reminder to self: easy on the irony among geeks.=A0 I pretty clearly said t=
hat Lojban is capable of being used for philosophy, though I did question w=
hy one would want to.=A0 Not doing so is (again rather clearly) a matter on=
ly of good taste.=A0 As for Sanskrit, it is created only in the sense of be=
ing a (slight) regularizing of the language of existing texts (some of the =
rics, for example are not quite Sanskrit, having wild forms.=A0 By the Veda=
nta everything is pretty much in place and thereafter Panini rules).=A0 Tho=
se texts are already religious moving toward philosophical so there is prob=
ably no way to keep it from going on in that way (even the Kamasutra reads =
like a theology manual, and also much of the epics).=A0 So, go, do philosop=
hy -- but figutre out how to order a pound of butter and a dozen eggs first=
=A0 (or last, of course -- after satori, the dishes).



